 been walked by the legs belonging to these two gents. For Eric Hall (left) it was fifty years since his first turn-out in a Belgrave '7'. He placed 140th that day in 1948 (31st Belgravian home with another two behind him) in a race won by Harry Churcher. George Beecham (right) will be celebrating the half a century since his début in this race in 2000.","id":"B227-116","w":"March 1999"}],"photo":{"file":"crops/B146/B146-p14-london-brighton-walk.jpg","caption":"BOTTOM LEFT: Belgrave's winning London Brighton Walk team seen passing through Clapham. K. Bailey (7th) G. Beecham (9th) R.Hall (6th [illegible]","source":"B146-29","when":"January 1962"},"x":1,"share":{"d":"George Beecham in The Belgravian, the Belgrave Harriers club gazette, 1960–2006: 195 mentions in 84 issues, 122 race results and 4 photographs. Wrote or reported 2 items.","img":"https://belgravian-images.stephendgardner.workers.dev/belgravian/crops/B146/B146-p14-london-brighton-walk.jpg","u":"https://stephengardner1.github.io/belgrave-harriers-data/belgravian/read/share/p-george-beecham.html"},"legend":false}